WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:06.500
In Season 5 of Game of Thrones, Tyrion Lannister
and Jorah Mormont are attacked by stone

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.610
men in the ruins of Valyria. Stone men
are people with a disease called greyscale,

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.650
which makes the skin “grey and cracked and
hard” and “stiff and dead” like stone,

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:21.290
eventually causing madness then death. The disease develops slowly, usually starting

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:25.820
on a finger or toe then spreading across the skin. There are said to be “three good

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:31.510
cures for greyscale: axe and sword and cleaver.
Hacking off afflicted parts … sometimes

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:35.940
stop[s] the spread of the disease … but
not always”. Greyscale is highly contagious

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:40.719
– just touching a stone man can spread the
sickness, and this is what happens to Jorah

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:46.050
in the show, and Jon Connington in the books.
George R. R. Martin describes this as a “death

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:52.620
sentence”, but a slow one – you can survive
years with greyscale, but death is inevitable.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.730
There are other forms of greyscale, though,
one of which is often seen in children, who

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:00.859
may actually survive the disease but be left
disfigured, which is what happens to Shireen

00:01:00.859 --> 00:01:05.390
Baratheon. Surviving childhood greyscale is
said to protect you from getting it again,

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:10.070
though in the books the wildling Val says
that “The grey death sleeps, only to wake

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:14.470
again”, which kinda implies that the disease
can come back.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.070
In any case, greyscale is pretty rare in Westeros,
but it’s apparently more common in Volantis

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:22.890
and the cities of the Rhoyne, who send people
with greyscale to “the ruins of Valyria”

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.920
in the show, and to the Sorrows in the books,
where the stone men wander “through the

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.880
fog until they die”. Some believe that
the stone men of the Sorrows are ruled by

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:37.360
someone called the Shrouded Lord who gives
“grey kiss[es]” and resides over a “stony

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:42.750
court”. One story says this Lord was once
a statue, until “a grey woman came out of

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:47.230
the fog and kissed him with lips as cold as
ice”. Which sounds kinda like the white

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:51.920
walkers and wights. Might there be a connection
between the zombies of ice and the zombies

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:56.500
of stone? For now we don’t know.
What we do know is that the stone men are

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:01.370
people with greyscale, which Shireen had,
and Jorah slash Jon Conn now has – making

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:07.780
him a dying man with nothing to lose.
Thanks for watching. There’ll be more theories

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:11.299
and analyses ahead, but let me know if you’d
like to see more of these little explanations

00:02:11.299 --> 00:02:11.680
too.

